@startuml
title What a saga scenario test controls and what it observes

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

component "Scenario test" as T #FFF8E1

package "Under test" #F4F7F9 {
  component "Order service" as O
  component "Inventory service" as I
  component "Payment service" as P
  component "Cart, catalog,\nnotification" as R
}

queue "Bus" as BUS
component "Gate\none per consumer:\nforwards, holds, releases,\nrepeats a message" as G #FFE0B2
component "Simulated payment provider\nan adapter of the payment service:\nanswers by token, records every call" as PSP #E3F2FD
component "Simulated e-mail provider\nan adapter of the notification service:\nrecords every e-mail" as MAIL #E3F2FD
component "Observation subscriptions\none per topic" as OBS #C8E6C9

T --> O : places an order,\ndecides as an administrator
T ..> G : holds and releases\na type of message
T ..> I : freezes, kills, starts
T ..> P : freezes, kills, starts
T ..> PSP : chooses the token,\nends a blackout
O --> BUS
I --> BUS
P --> BUS
BUS --> G
G --> O
G --> I
G --> P
G --> R
P --> PSP
R --> MAIL
BUS --> OBS
T <-- OBS : every message, in order
T <-- PSP : how many charges,\ncancellations, refunds
T <-- MAIL : which e-mails
T <-- O : status of the order,\nwhat its saga knows

note bottom of G
  The gate exists in the composition of containers only.
  No service knows it is there: each one reads
  a subscription whose name is configuration.
end note
@enduml
